eye-contact-co-processing-at-the-speed-of-light-lines-4 : List (List Word)
eye-contact-co-processing-at-the-speed-of-light-lines-4 = cons "Your Brain Is Exposed to the World" (cons (quoted (cons "Here's a fact that should be more widely known: your eyes are not separate organs " (cons "plugged into" (cons " your brain. They are your brain, extended outward." nil)))) (cons (quoted (cons "The retina develops embryologically as an outgrowth of the brain itself—specifically from the diencephalon during early development. What we call the " (cons "eye" (cons " is actually brain tissue (central nervous system) that migrated out during fetal development to sample the electromagnetic field directly." nil)))) (cons "When an ophthalmologist examines your retina, they're looking at your central nervous system. Not through it, not connected to it—they're directly observing neural tissue that processes information. The blood vessels visible in your retina are supplying brain tissue. The layers of cells performing edge detection, motion sensing, and contrast enhancement are performing computation in what is literally your nervous system." (cons "This means: Your nervous system is directly exposed to the outside world. Light doesn't travel to a sensor that then sends signals to your brain. Light directly strikes brain tissue and is immediately transduced to neural activations—the quotient operation from photon flux to neural firing patterns happens in exposed nervous tissue." nil))))
